  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Quest Diagnostics obligated $53.6M in federal contracts in FY2027 to date. Quest Diagnostics received 61 awards so far in the fiscal year, with an average award size of $878K. Quest Diagnostics obligations are down 20.8% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations declined from $194M in FY22 to $53.6M in FY27, with intermediate totals of $138M in FY23, $98.7M in FY24, $50.7M in FY25, and $67.6M in FY26. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer of Quest Diagnostics services in FY2027 to date, obligating $53.8M. Medical Laboratories is the largest market for Quest Diagnostics in FY2027 to date, with $53.4M obligated. The facts page notes that all figures are contract obligations except award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables, and that current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Quest Diagnostics’ federal business trended recently?",
        "body": "Quest Diagnostics obligations fell from $194M in FY22 to $53.6M in FY27. Quest Diagnostics obligations are down 20.8% year over year, with annual totals of $138M in FY23, $98.7M in FY24, $50.7M in FY25, and $67.6M in FY26."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the main federal buyers and markets for Quest Diagnostics?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $53.8M to Quest Diagnostics in FY2027 to date. Medical Laboratories is the primary market for Quest Diagnostics with $53.4M in obligations, followed by In-Vitro Diagnostic Substance Manufacturing at $144K and Research and Development in the Social Sciences and Humanities at $24.6K."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Quest Diagnostics make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Quest Diagnostics made $53.6M from federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Quest Diagnostics received 61 awards so far in the fiscal year and the average award size was $878K, and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date)."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Quest Diagnostics?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs buys the most from Quest Diagnostics, obligating $53.8M in FY2027 to date. Other agencies appear in the buyer list in the supplied facts, but the Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer in the current-year snapshot."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Quest Diagnostics sell to the government?",
      "a": "Quest Diagnostics sells medical laboratory services and diagnostic-related products to the government, as shown by $53.4M in Medical Laboratories obligations in FY2027 to date. Quest Diagnostics also has obligations in In-Vitro Diagnostic Substance Manufacturing at $144K and Research and Development in the Social Sciences and Humanities at $24.6K."
    },
